@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] complete-build-inputs
An action's key MUST cover its code, data, declared settings and consumed product identities.
Order-only and reference edges MUST NOT hide reads of derived data. Missing required inputs and
incomplete outputs MUST NOT be treated as a cache hit. Explicit optional files MUST carry a distinct
absent identity when missing, so their appearance, removal and content changes invalidate consumers.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] independent-artifact-ownership
A named product MUST have one owner and a complete byte inventory. Restored outputs MUST be
independent copies; a failed or interrupted restoration MUST NOT leave a successful build stamp.
Native Unreal packages MUST NOT opt into a portable cache until their relocation contract passes.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] advisory-capacity
The capacity planner MUST NOT write scheduler state, grant leases, take locks, launch workloads or
change the live safety system. A queued phase MUST hold no resources or named locks.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] gated-private-service-ownership
Shared Zen/Trace services and their descendants MUST remain excluded from accounting and signals
unless a fresh direct child of the exact guarded compound driver was explicitly spawned behind an
invocation-private exec gate. Its exact PID/start identity MUST be bound to both launcher tracking
and the independent aggregate monitor, with live aggregate and actual-child guard readiness, before
GO. Default behavior MUST have no exceptions. Arbitrary PID adoption, post-exec registration,
PID-reuse inheritance and public mutable allowlists MUST NOT grant ownership. Lost registration,
acknowledgment or guard telemetry MUST fail closed and retain ordinary pinned cleanup/admission.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;safety] stable-logical-task-fresh-reports
A fixed legacy provider MAY bind logical_folder to the original actual task/kind/checkout folder
string when each invocation uses a fresh physical report namespace. It MUST replace ONLY the
existing folder ingredient in UUID5 request identity, without canonicalization, new UUID/priority,
ready-time or resource/profile/admission changes. None MUST preserve existing behavior. Every
internal no-GO retry MUST receive the same logical identity; actual reports MUST stay under the
fresh physical folder. Provider history MUST distinguish actual raw/failed peaks and verified
completed metrics, never manufacture successful peak or cleanup evidence from a locator. See
test_fresh_report_names_keep_original_logical_identity_and_resource_request and
test_logical_folder_survives_every_internal_requeue_while_reports_stay_fresh.
